From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: motorcomm: T32 PRJ007 YT8512 in RMII like U-Boot

The PRJ007 module's PHY reads id 0x00000128 (YT8512, driver "sz18201").
Its config_init cleared ext reg 0x50 bit 6 and left Rmii_en to the strap,
and Linux got no carrier, while the thingino U-Boot (motorcomm.c
yt8512_config: ext 0x4000 Rmii_en|RX_DV_sel, ext 0x50 bit 6 set, soft
reset) gets a 100/full link and a DHCP lease on the same cable
(openimp #849). Do the same on PRJ007; other SoCs are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/motorcomm.c
@@ -61,15 +61,27 @@
 
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1e, 0x50);
 	reg = phy_read(phydev, 0x1f);
-	/* bit6, 1:50M 0:25M */
+	/*
+	 * bit6: PLL reference select. T32 PRJ007 (YT8512, id 0x128, RMII
+	 * with the 50 MHz REF_CLK from the MAC): the thingino U-Boot sets it
+	 * (motorcomm.c yt8512_config) and gets a link; cleared the PHY never
+	 * negotiates (openimp #849).
+	 */
+#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_PRJ007
+	reg |= 0x40;
+#else
 	reg &= ~0x40;
-	// reg |= 0x40;
+#endif
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1f, reg);
 
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1e, 0x4000);
 	reg = phy_read(phydev, 0x1f);
 	// reg = 0x13;
 	reg |= 0x10;
+#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_PRJ007
+	/* Rmii_en: do not trust the RX_DV strap (MII on a weak pull-up). */
+	reg |= 0x02;
+#endif
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1f, reg);
 #if 1 // Drive
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1e, 0x2012);
@@ -93,6 +105,25 @@
 	reg |= 0x10;
 	phy_write(phydev, 0x1f, reg);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_SOC_PRJ007
+	/*
+	 * Interface and PLL settings take effect after a soft reset; the
+	 * extended registers survive it (as U-Boot yt8512_config does).
+	 */
+	{
+		int i;
+
+		phy_write(phydev, MII_BMCR, BMCR_RESET);
+		for (i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
+			reg = phy_read(phydev, MII_BMCR);
+			if (reg >= 0 && !(reg & BMCR_RESET))
+				break;
+			mdelay(5);
+		}
+		phy_write(phydev, MII_BMCR, 0x3100);
+	}
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
